[[:db/retract 17592186086232 :answer-field/choices 17592186086233] [:db/retract 17592186086232 :answer-field/choices 17592186086234] [:db/retract 17592186086232 :answer-field/choices 17592186086235] [:db/retract 17592186086232 :answer-field/choices 17592186086236] [:db/retract 17592186086232 :answer-field/choices 17592186086237] {:db/id 17592186087689 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-06bb1232-0a8a-5e1c-9d8b-cb06e8535b98" "question-d0fb4c30-2477-5421-b3da-f8a97304168e"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186087494 :question/problem "What is the value of $x$ if $e^{x - 3}=2^5?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we take the natural logarithm $\\left(\\ln\\right)$ of both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x-3} & ={2}^{5} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{x-3}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({2}^{5})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the fact that $\\ln \\left( e^a \\right) = a$ to simplify the left-hand side. This gives\n\n$$\nx-3 = \\ln \\left( 2^5 \\right).\n$$\n\nFinally, we solve for $x$ and rewrite the right-hand side using the power law of logarithms, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-3 & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({2}^{5}) \\\\ x & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({2}^{5})+3 \\\\ x & =5\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)+3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=5\\ln (2) + 3.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186087690 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-f830d198-6965-5666-82fb-312c594f3381"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186087495 :question/worked-solution "First, we take the natural logarithm $(\\ln)$ of both sides of the equation and solve for $x\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2-4x} & =2 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{2-4x}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2) \\\\ 2-4x & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2) \\\\ -4x & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)-2 \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating the above expression using a calculator gives\n\n$$\nx  \\approx 0.327\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places." :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186087691 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-75357678-4591-5397-a921-c421db4eafd8"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186087496 :question/problem "Given that $e^{x+1} + 1 = 3,$ what is the value of $x$?" :question/worked-solution "First, we isolate the exponential, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x+1}+1 & =3 \\\\ {e}^{x+1} & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we find the natural logarithm $\\left(\\ln\\right)$ of both sides of the equation and solve for $x\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x+1} & =2 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{x+1}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2) \\\\ x+1 & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2) \\\\ x & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x =\\ln\\left(2\\right) -1.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-06bb1232-0a8a-5e1c-9d8b-cb06e8535b98" :question/id #uuid "06bb1232-0a8a-5e1c-9d8b-cb06e8535b98" :question/math-academy-id "q-100280" :question/problem "What is the value of $y$ if ${e}^{7-y}=\\sqrt[7]{10}?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the natural logarithm $(ln)$ of both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{7-y} & =\\sqrt[7]{10} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{7-y}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\sqrt[7]{10})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the fact that $\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{a})=a$ to simplify the left-hand side. This gives:\n\n$$\n7-y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\sqrt[7]{10})\n$$\n\nNext, we write $\\sqrt[7]{10}$ as ${10}^{1/7}.$ So, we get:\n\n$$\n7-y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({10}^{1/7})\n$$\n\nFinally, we rewrite the right-hand side using power law of logarithms and solve for $y,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7-y & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({10}^{1/7}) \\\\ 7-y & =\\frac{1}{7}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(10) \\\\ -y & =\\frac{1}{7}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(10)-7 \\\\ y & =7-\\frac{1}{7}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(10)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $y=7-\\frac{1}{7}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(10).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-4636930a-45e4-5386-a94d-82184908cb41"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-4636930a-45e4-5386-a94d-82184908cb41" :answer-field/id #uuid "4636930a-45e4-5386-a94d-82184908cb41" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-7f8797e5-9480-5a81-814e-1bfb99aec85f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e7d5168f-0f24-5fcf-8392-ea9fd185e22d" "answer-de0f44c4-a8d6-56ea-afc9-b58f1f9e5239" "answer-63b2ed40-cb9c-56e8-a73c-1fb3a500de4b" "answer-143cf35a-845a-521f-9117-ce3541756c04" "answer-7f8797e5-9480-5a81-814e-1bfb99aec85f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e7d5168f-0f24-5fcf-8392-ea9fd185e22d" :answer/id #uuid "e7d5168f-0f24-5fcf-8392-ea9fd185e22d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=1+\\frac{1}{7}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(10)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-de0f44c4-a8d6-56ea-afc9-b58f1f9e5239" :answer/id #uuid "de0f44c4-a8d6-56ea-afc9-b58f1f9e5239" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=1-\\frac{1}{10}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(7)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-63b2ed40-cb9c-56e8-a73c-1fb3a500de4b" :answer/id #uuid "63b2ed40-cb9c-56e8-a73c-1fb3a500de4b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=10+\\frac{1}{7}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(10)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-143cf35a-845a-521f-9117-ce3541756c04" :answer/id #uuid "143cf35a-845a-521f-9117-ce3541756c04" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=7-\\frac{1}{10}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(7)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7f8797e5-9480-5a81-814e-1bfb99aec85f" :answer/id #uuid "7f8797e5-9480-5a81-814e-1bfb99aec85f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=7-\\frac{1}{7}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(10)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-d0fb4c30-2477-5421-b3da-f8a97304168e" :question/id #uuid "d0fb4c30-2477-5421-b3da-f8a97304168e" :question/math-academy-id "q-100276" :question/problem "What is the value of $y$ if ${e}^{5-y}=\\sqrt[4]{7}?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the natural logarithm $(ln)$ of both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{5-y} & =\\sqrt[4]{7} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{5-y}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\sqrt[4]{7})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the fact that $\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{a})=a$ to simplify the left-hand side. This gives:\n\n$$\n5-y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\sqrt[4]{7})\n$$\n\nNext, we write $\\sqrt[4]{7}$ as ${7}^{1/4}.$ So, we get:\n\n$$\n5-y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({7}^{1/4})\n$$\n\nFinally, we rewrite the right-hand side using power law of logarithms and solve for $y,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5-y & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({7}^{1/4}) \\\\ 5-y & =\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(7) \\\\ -y & =\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(7)-5 \\\\ y & =5-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(7)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $y=5-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(7).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-a12fa105-d919-568d-aa42-9d5dd1b4d2a4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a12fa105-d919-568d-aa42-9d5dd1b4d2a4" :answer-field/id #uuid "a12fa105-d919-568d-aa42-9d5dd1b4d2a4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-13714b98-7f8c-58e4-884c-b96dd8f0deff" :answer-field/choices ["answer-02492c1c-263a-53d5-a2ab-a44b808ad394" "answer-e39eb702-bd3e-5d40-bf2a-84989610b7f7" "answer-110732bb-df28-569e-8e30-9e1291e4a0dd" "answer-4066d5e8-82e4-5526-876f-28005ec446fb" "answer-13714b98-7f8c-58e4-884c-b96dd8f0deff"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-02492c1c-263a-53d5-a2ab-a44b808ad394" :answer/id #uuid "02492c1c-263a-53d5-a2ab-a44b808ad394" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=3-\\frac{1}{14}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(7)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e39eb702-bd3e-5d40-bf2a-84989610b7f7" :answer/id #uuid "e39eb702-bd3e-5d40-bf2a