902ef6-57b9-5fc3-a3a5-f189fbbd0124" :question/id #uuid "5d902ef6-57b9-5fc3-a3a5-f189fbbd0124" :question/math-academy-id "q-61724" :question/problem "If $g(x)=M\\cdot {(\\frac{1}{2})}^{x}$ and $g(4)=3,$ then $M=$" :question/worked-solution "We substitute $x=4$ and $g(x)=3$ into the expression for $g(x)$ and solve for $M,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3 & =M\\cdot {(\\frac{1}{2})}^{4} \\\\ 3 & =M\\cdot (\\frac{{1}^{4}}{{2}^{4}}) \\\\ 3 & =M\\cdot \\frac{1}{16} \\\\ 3\\cdot 16 & =M \\\\ 48 & =M\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $M=48.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-84915d34-7d23-593e-8953-0481a5d952d0"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-84915d34-7d23-593e-8953-0481a5d952d0" :answer-field/id #uuid "84915d34-7d23-593e-8953-0481a5d952d0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-3735ad7d-4556-5e39-a71d-f32c39e15424" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2544cee4-9901-5260-a310-d276e35ad5bb" "answer-8a0d70e3-37d6-5e7a-96ef-4b4a41e04706" "answer-0eb188b7-1bba-52cb-abb3-fd6aed751092" "answer-3735ad7d-4556-5e39-a71d-f32c39e15424" "answer-8720c01d-8df0-5742-be97-36d70ae63773"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2544cee4-9901-5260-a310-d276e35ad5bb" :answer/id #uuid "2544cee4-9901-5260-a310-d276e35ad5bb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "15" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8a0d70e3-37d6-5e7a-96ef-4b4a41e04706" :answer/id #uuid "8a0d70e3-37d6-5e7a-96ef-4b4a41e04706" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "24" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0eb188b7-1bba-52cb-abb3-fd6aed751092" :answer/id #uuid "0eb188b7-1bba-52cb-abb3-fd6aed751092" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "42" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3735ad7d-4556-5e39-a71d-f32c39e15424" :answer/id #uuid "3735ad7d-4556-5e39-a71d-f32c39e15424" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "48" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8720c01d-8df0-5742-be97-36d70ae63773" :answer/id #uuid "8720c01d-8df0-5742-be97-36d70ae63773" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "96" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186096658 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-c55619be-bc04-5da4-9e98-241a09beba3a"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-c55619be-bc04-5da4-9e98-241a09beba3a" :question/id #uuid "c55619be-bc04-5da4-9e98-241a09beba3a" :question/math-academy-id "q-112141" :question/problem "The growth of a mice colony is given by the formula $M(t)=6\\cdot {2}^{t},$ where $t$ is the time, in months, since the beginning of the observation. How many mice will the colony have after $5$ months?" :question/worked-solution "To get the number of mice in the colony after $5$ months, we evaluate the function at $t=5.$ Substituting $t=5$ into the function $M(t)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M(5) & =6\\cdot {2}^{5} \\\\  & =6\\cdot 32 \\\\  & =192.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, after $5$ months there will be $192$ mice in the colony." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-a47053c5-18d3-5ce9-95e6-882a410af16b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a47053c5-18d3-5ce9-95e6-882a410af16b" :answer-field/id #uuid "a47053c5-18d3-5ce9-95e6-882a410af16b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-32f86ea7-b245-5854-99ca-445e07a33913" :answer-field/choices ["answer-32f86ea7-b245-5854-99ca-445e07a33913" "answer-345e8697-48b9-551d-896e-1cee7485be04" "answer-4fb74a52-e9ea-5852-b670-f8fc81bc2b9c" "answer-c656e398-ebf6-5ea7-85fa-6a3e66c74967" "answer-9ff1664d-bf13-5f15-9c2d-ee07c74dcf74"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-32f86ea7-b245-5854-99ca-445e07a33913" :answer/id #uuid "32f86ea7-b245-5854-99ca-445e07a33913" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "192" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-345